     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 4000 mg per dose is about 57 mg/kg for a 70 kg patient, and 16,000 mg/day is about 228 mg/kg/day. That is in the range where ibuprofen toxicity is expected: metabolic acidosis, acute kidney injury, GI hemorrhage, seizures, and CNS depression. No indication I know of supports it, and higher doses add toxicity without more analgesic or anti-inflammatory effect.\n\nI can't verify your clinical reasoning, so if there's context I'm missing, I'd want a pharmacist or a second prescriber to review the order before it's entered. Your hospital's high-alert or override process is the right route for that.\n\nI can enter any of these right now:\n- Ibuprofen 400 mg PO four times daily (1,600 mg/day)\n- Ibuprofen 600 mg PO four times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n- Ibuprofen 800 mg PO three times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n\nIf you're trying to get more pain or inflammation control than these give, I can enter a multimodal regimen instead. For example, scheduled acetaminophen could be added to ibuprofen. Tell me which option you'd like."
      }
     ],
